<title>FRANCE: French sugar consumption rose in September - FIRS.</title>
<headline>French sugar consumption rose in September - FIRS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>French sugar consumption rose to a provisional 206,000 tonnes in September from a revised 153,000 tonnes in August, the FIRS sugar intervention board said on Thursday.</p>
<p>But consumption was down from 208,133 tonnes in September 1995, FIRS said in its November report.</p>
<p>This would bring cumulative sales to the French market for the full 1995/96 (October/September) campaign to 2.011 million tonnes against 2.006 million in 1994/95.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 421432</p>
</text>
